+# Story RC3.2: Message Templates & Send Helpers
+
+Status: review
+
+Epic: RC3 (Reference-Checking — Messaging & Collection) · Story key: `rc3-2-message-templates-send-helpers`
+Sprint: refcheck-v1 (tracker: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status-refcheck-v1.yaml`)
+
+## Story
+
+As a referee,
+I want clear, honest messages that tell me who is asking, why, and what my rights are,
+so that I can trust the link, or decline it, with full information.
+
+## Scope (what THIS story owns — and what it does NOT)
+
+**Owns (templates + the helpers the sweep calls):**
+
+1. `server/src/reference_checks/messages.gleam` — the pure template builders (the copy contract): T0 invite (email + SMS), T+24h applicant co-nudge (email), T+48h reminder 1 (email + SMS), T+96h reminder 2 (email + SMS), T+96h landlord warm-handoff (email with the attempt log rendered). Plus the URL builders (`form_url`, `stop_url`, `notice_url`) and the per-channel `ChannelOutcome` type the attempt log consumes.
+2. `server/src/reference_checks/send.gleam` — the send helpers (`send_invite`, `send_reminder`, `send_co_nudge`, `send_warm_handoff`) that call rc3-1's `sms_client` (Alpha Sender ID "RTenantry", status-callback URL already wired in the client) and the existing `email_client`, no-op-safe without keys.
+3. Unit tests for both modules.
+
+**Does NOT own (later stories — do not build them):**
+
+- **The cadence sweep** (which rows are due, when each step fires, the guarded DB update, token minting + `form_token_expires_at` TTL stamping) → **rc3-5**. This story's helpers take an already-minted `form_token` as input (see Decisions).
+- **The `/reference/:token` form route** (GET/POST, autosave, expiry pages) → **rc3-3**.
+- **The `/reference/:token/stop` route** (GET confirm page, POST objection), the in-form decline route, and the `reference_objection_log` writer → **rc3-4**. rc3-2 only embeds the stop-link URL in every template — the URL path itself is the fixed AD-6 contract.
+- **The notification-dispatcher integration** (in-app notifications, `notification_preference` plumbing, FR-RC15) → **rc4-4**. rc3-2's warm-handoff helper sends the landlord EMAIL only (architecture §8.3: "warm-handoff emails include the attempt log rendered").
+- **The Twilio delivery-callback webhook** (`/webhooks/twilio-sms`) → **rc3-6**. The callback URL already rides every send via rc3-1's client.
+- **No DB access at all.** No migration, no Squirrel regen. The helpers read no rows and write no rows; the sweep owns every write (AD-14).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epics, with the 2026-08-08 amendment applied)
+
+**AC1 — T0 invite carries the full Art 14 block (email) and the short notice + stop-link (SMS).**
+Given the copy deck (UX §6.2/§6.3, verbatim modulo the documented deviations below), when templates render with fixture data, then the invitation email carries: controller identity (`{landlord_display_name}`), RightTenantry as processor, source (the applicant), purpose + legitimate-interest basis, retention in plain terms, rights including objection, and the notice URL (`/privacy#referee-data`) — the architecture §9.1 required list. The invitation SMS carries the short notice + notice link + the stop-link.
+**Amendment note (2026-08-08, supersedes the epics' "Reply STOP to opt out"):** every SMS template carries the token-gated **stop-link** (`/reference/:token/stop`), NOT "reply STOP" — the Alpha Sender ID is one-way (AD-6 corrected, PR #593 amendment). The email "Decline" links also point to the stop-link (see Decisions).
+
+**AC2 — Reminders 1–2 + co-nudge render with the decline route and notice link.**
+Given UX §6.4/§10.1, when reminders 1–2 and the applicant co-nudge render with fixtures, then each referee message carries the form link + the stop-link (SMS) / decline link (email), the reminder emails repeat the notice link, and the copy matches the deck (verbatim modulo the documented deviations). The co-nudge goes to the APPLICANT (email only, AD-4) and carries no stop-link.
+
+**AC3 — Sender config + service-message discipline.**
+When a message is sent, then referee email goes from `references@righttenantry.ie` (OQ-11, existing verified transactional domain) and SMS from sender ID `RTenantry` (OQ-6, via rc3-1's client — there is no from-number). No message contains promotional content (ePrivacy service-message discipline, UX §6.1).
+
+**AC4 — Per-channel outcomes shaped for the attempt log.**
+Given the send helpers (`send_invite`, `send_reminder`, `send_co_nudge`, `send_warm_handoff`), when the sweep calls them, then each returns a per-channel outcome list (`ChannelOutcome(channel, outcome, detail)` with `channel ∈ {email, sms}` and `outcome ∈ {delivered, skipped, failed}`) shaped for the row's `attempts` JSONB (`[{at, channel, outcome, detail}]`; the sweep stamps `at`). `delivered` carries the provider id (Resend email id / Twilio message SID) in `detail`; `failed` carries the reason; `skipped` covers both no-keys and no-contact-on-that-channel.
+
+**AC5 — Graceful no-op without keys.**
+Without Twilio keys (sms_client `Disabled`) or a Resend key (`""`), the helpers no-op per channel with a log line and a `skipped` outcome — never crash a caller, never Sentry-capture the no-op (expected config state). Real provider API failures return `failed` outcomes; the sms_client's own Sentry capture (rc3-1) covers SMS; email failures get a `wisp.log_error` (the email_client precedent).
+
+**Verify:** unit tests render every template with fixtures asserting each Art 14 required element + the stop-link presence in every SMS + no `\u{2014}` (em-dash) in any user-facing string; send-helper tests assert the sms_client/email_client payload wiring (mocked per existing patterns — pure builders + the Disabled/""-key no-op branches); copy matches the pinned strings in this spec; `make test-server` green.
+
