+### The three documented deviations (review-visible)
+
+1. **Em-dash ban (RT global, briefing-asserted).** The UX deck uses ` — ` throughout; every instance converts to a colon (subjects), a full stop (sentence joins), or a comma (appositives). Tests pin `\u{2014}`-absence on every built string. The epics' "verbatim" AC yields to the global ban (the briefing explicitly re-asserts it for this story).
+2. **Stop-link amendment (2026-08-08, architecture amendments register).** "Reply STOP to opt out" (§6.3) and "or reply STOP" (§6.4) are DEAD — the one-way Alpha Sender ID cannot receive replies. Every SMS carries the stop-link instead. Additionally, the email "Decline here" links point to the SAME stop-link: the briefing ("the referee taps it to decline/object") collapses the message-originated decline onto the stop-link, the only pinned make-it-stop web route (AD-6). Consequence: a message-originated stop lands `objected` (hard stop, Art 21 evidence) rather than `refused` — strictly stronger GDPR posture; the `refused` path remains on the form landing (rc3-4). Flagged for review: if a distinct message-side `refused` route is wanted, rc3-4 must pin `/reference/:token/decline` first and these templates swap one href.
+3. **Slot-neutral phrasing.** The deck is landlord-ref-shaped ("gave us your details as her previous landlord", "about Aisling's tenancy"). Templates parameterise: `role_phrase(slot)` and a slot-neutral "confirm a few details about {applicant_first_name}" (drops "tenancy"/"employment" — honest for all three slots). Pronoun `her` → `their` (no sex data; protected-characteristics care).
+
+### Decisions & rationale (for the PR + future minions)
+
+1. **Token minting is rc3-5's, not this story's.** `insert_reference_call_if_absent` does not mint `form_token`; A3's TTL runs "10 days from invitation"; AD-14 makes the sweep the single writer. So the T0 guarded update mints the token + stamps `form_token_expires_at` (precedent: `wisp.random_string(48)` = ~288-bit, `application_handler.insert_erasure_token`), and this story's helpers take the minted token as input. Keeps rc3-2 DB-free.
+2. **Two modules, not one.** Epics name `messages.gleam (+ templates)`; the 200-line logic-module target + the pure/IO split argue for `messages.gleam` (pure builders, the copy contract) + `send.gleam` (the helpers calling email_client/sms_client). Mirrors rc3-1's one-concern-per-module outcome.
+3. **`SendDeps` record over `ServerConfig`.** The helpers need exactly three things (resend key, twilio handle, sentry handle). Taking `ServerConfig` would couple a pure-messaging module to the whole server config and make unit tests construct a 20-field record. The sweep assembles `SendDeps` from config in one line. Rejected: passing three positional args (unlabelled trios rot fast); rejected: `ServerConfig` (test weight + coupling).
+4. **Two senders.** Referee-facing mail (invite, reminders) from `RightTenantry References <references@righttenantry.ie>` (OQ-11's verified-domain decision). Applicant-facing co-nudge + landlord-facing warm handoff from the established `RightTenantry <noreply@app.righttenantry.ie>` — those audiences' existing transactional sender; OQ-11 scoped `references@` to referee mail. Flagged for Perkins r1.
+5. **`expiry_date` passed in as a formatted string.** The sweep knows `form_token_expires_at`; formatting a timestamptz for humans is the caller's (the `format_close_date` precedent: emails receive pre-formatted date strings). `""` → reminder-2 copy falls back to "10 days from our first message" (true under A3 regardless).
+6. **No UTM tracking on referee links.** `email_client.tracked_application_url` is the application-funnel mechanism; referee links are capability-token URLs whose query strings would ride PostHog autocapture (the token-leak review finding, 2026-08-03). The form/stop/notice links go out bare.
+7. **Email HTML built locally, not by exporting email_client privates.** `email_wrapper`/`cta_button`/`email_divider`/`fallback_link` are private. Widening email_client's API for this story would touch a module under active use; the reference templates build the same minimal inline-styled markup locally (table/inline-style only, no classes) and import only the already-public `escape_html`, `send_email_with_tags`. If a third email family appears, extract a shared `email_markup` module then (not now).
+8. **`List-Unsubscribe` NOT added.** These are service messages (Art 14 notice vehicle), not marketing; the stop-link IS the opt-out mechanism, token-bound per referee. Adding a mailto-unsubscribe would create an unlogged objection channel (AD-6 wants evidence).
+
+### Pattern fidelity — mirror these exactly
+
+- **`notification/sms_client.gleam`** (rc3-1, merged #594): `send_sms(twilio:, sentry:, to:, body:)` returns `Result(SendOutcome, String)` with `Sent(message_sid)` / `Skipped`. The Alpha Sender ID + status-callback URL are already inside the client — helpers pass only `to`/`body`.
+- **`notification/email_client.gleam`**: `send_email_with_tags(api_key, from, to, subject, html, tags)` returns `Result(email_id, String)`. Empty-key skip precedent: `application_detail_handler.gleam:784` (`wisp.log_warning` + skip, no Sentry).
+- **Attempt-log vocabulary** (`20260731222000_create_reference_call.sql:101`): `attempts JSONB [{at, channel, outcome, detail}]` — `ChannelOutcome` maps 1:1 minus `at` (the sweep stamps `at` when it builds the guarded append, `append_reference_call_attempt.sql`).
+- **No-op honesty (AC5):** skips log one line and return `skipped` outcomes; only real provider failures are `failed`. Never crash the sweep (AD-15's silent-death prohibition is about the sweep itself; helpers must never be the reason a tick dies).
+
+### Constraints (RT-specific — APPLY here)
+
+- **No em-dashes in user-facing copy** — every subject, SMS body, and email HTML string gets a `\u{2014}`-absence test (the `welcome_html_has_no_em_dash_test` precedent).
+- **Every SMS template includes the stop-link** (`/reference/:token/stop`), never "reply STOP" (AD-6 corrected).
+- **The Art 14 notice** rides the T0 invite (full block in email, short notice + links in SMS) per architecture §9.1's required list.
+- **SMS FROM "RTenantry"** via rc3-1's client — no from-number, no `TWILIO_FROM`.
+- **Graceful no-op without keys** (AC5) — `make test-server` green with no Twilio/Resend env set (CI runs exactly that).
+- **No promotional content, ever** (UX §6.1) — a marketing line converts a lawful service message into regulated direct marketing.
+- **No `let assert`** in production code; **no JavaScript FFI**; **no new deps** (`gleam/json`, `gleam/string`, `gleam/option`, `wisp`, `notification/email_client`, `notification/sms_client`, `sentry/sentry_client` all present).
+- **Escape every interpolated value** with `email_client.escape_html` (referee/applicant/landlord names are user-controlled; they land in HTML emails).
+- **Capability-token hygiene:** tokens appear ONLY in the full `form_url`/`stop_url` link hrefs/bodies — never in logs, Sentry messages, subjects, or `detail` strings (the attempt log is landlord-visible). The token-redaction registry (`middleware.redact_token_route`) covers `/reference/*` server-side; the helpers must not add a second leak path.
